  "lineage": "Traditional music of Asturias in northern Spain, documented by Eduardo Martínez Torner's 1920 Cancionero musical and revived from the 1980s by Llan de Cubel and the Xixón folk scene — the single-drone gaita asturiana in B-flat playing giraldillas and muñeiras against snare-and-bass-drum tamboriteru, and the tonada or asturianada, a solo unmetred song delivered at full chest voice with long melismatic ornaments and heavy portamento.",
